    "knowledge_point": "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Secant Function",
    "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y={5}^{x}sec⁡x.$",
    "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({5}^{x}sec⁡x) \\\\  & ={5}^{x}ln⁡5sec⁡x+{5}^{x}sec⁡xtan⁡x \\\\  & ={5}^{x}sec⁡x(ln⁡5+tan⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
